Paper 2 cites Paper 1 for them; repetition is not a defect.
BOILERPLATE rows are stock epistemic phrasing; the register is shared by
both papers and by the field.
SHARED-TERM rows are technical phrases both papers must use (the name of
an ablation, a state). Not a defect.
SUBSTANTIVE rows are the only ones that would count as self-plagiarism: a
whole clause (>= 40 characters, >= 6 content words) repeated verbatim.
There are none.

